{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To complement branches, Antora can be configured to use the worktree linked to any branch it discovers in a local repository. This behavior is controlled using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key. The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts a boolean value or a list of exact worktree names, name patterns, or symbolic names."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Worktrees are only relevant for branches, not tags."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key is optional. The key can be specified directly on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "content"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key (which changes the default value for all content sources) or on an individual content source (which overrides the inherited default value). The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts a boolean value or list. Each value in the list can be an exact worktree name (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "v2.3"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "main"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", etc.), a positive or negative name pattern (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "v2.*"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "v@({1..9})*({0..9}).({0..9}).x+"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", etc.), or a symbolic name (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). The list of name patterns can be any combination of these value types, with one caveat."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The worktrees key don’t select content itself. Instead, it makes worktrees available to be selected by the branches key. If the current branch of a worktree matches one of branches selected, then Antora uses the files from that worktree. So we can say that worktrees are used by association when their branch is selected."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "There are a few things to note about worktrees. Typically, a worktree has the same name as the branch from which it was created, but not always. The main worktree does not have a formal name and is therefore represented in Antora by the symbolic name "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (to symbolize the current directory at the main repository root)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The main worktree is not necessarily linked to the main branch. The fact that they are both use the term “main” is merely coincidental."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key is not specified, Antora automatically uses the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default filter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#default"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "worktrees-key",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "worktrees key"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key isn’t set on a content source, Antora use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "default worktrees filter"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "strong",
                "roles": [
                  "term"
                ]
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". That means Antora will use the main worktree of the (local) repository (represented as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") if the current branch of that worktree is selected by the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "branches"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " filter. If such a match is made, Antora uses the files from that worktree instead of the files from the git tree for that branch."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can override the default filter by setting the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key directly on the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "content"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " parent key."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "default",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Default worktrees filter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, Antora does not scan for linked worktrees. You can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to customize this behavior. To enable the use of all worktrees, simply set the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to the boolean value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "content:\n  sources:\n  - url: /path/to/repo-a/main\n    branches: [v1.0, v2.0, main]\n    worktrees: true"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Antora will discover linked worktrees regardless of whether the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "url"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " points to the main worktree or a linked worktree of the reository (or even the bare repository)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Antora supports using a linked worktree directly as a content source. (Antora discovers the corresponding git repository by following the .git file in that directory.) If you don’t specify the worktrees key, Antora automatically selects the current (linked) worktree. You can then use the files in that worktree by using "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "HEAD"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " as the value of the "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "branches"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " key."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "If you start from a linked worktree, and want to use the main worktree, then you can use the symbolic name "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "/."
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " to refer to the main worktree."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "section",
            "id": "linked-worktree-as-content-source",
            "level": 2,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Linked worktree as content source"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "use-all-worktrees",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Use all worktrees"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you want Antora to bypass all worktrees, set the value of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key to the keyword "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". In this case, Antora will always read files from the git tree."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "content:\n  sources:\n  - url: /path/to/repo-a/main\n    branches: [v1.0, v2.0, main]\n    worktrees: false"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "antora-playbook.yml"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "dont-use-any-worktrees",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Don’t use any worktrees"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "worktrees"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key accepts the following keyword values:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Use all worktrees (the main worktree and all linked worktrees)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "true"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Do not use any worktrees (not the main worktree or any linked worktrees)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "false (or ~)"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Use only the main worktree."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "/."
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Use only the current worktree. (default)"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "."
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Use only the linked worktrees."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "*"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The boolean values "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "true"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "false"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " can only be used as a singular value, not as an entry in the list. The symbolic names "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " cannot be negated."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If your repository only has a main worktree, then "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " act the same. If the content source points to a linked worktree, then "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " matches that worktree and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " must be used to match the main worktree."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "specify-worktrees-by-keyword",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Specify worktrees by keyword"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you want more fine-grained control over which worktrees Antora uses, you can specify a list of glob patterns. You refer to worktrees by their name, which is often the branch name to which they are linked (but not always). Thus, the glob pattern works the same as described on the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "content-branches.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "content-branches.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " page. If you want to refer to the current worktree, you do so using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " keyword. If you want to refer to the main worktree, you do so using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "/."
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " keyword."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Let’s configure Antora to use the main worktree as well as the linked worktree for the v2.0 branch. The files for the v1.0 branch will be read from the git tree, even if there is a linked worktree associated with that branch."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
